# Synchronization - Synchronisation
#
DoliCalSyncPhone                 = Sync my phone
DoliCalSyncIntro                 = Your DoliCal agenda in the calendar of your phone, your Mac or Thunderbird, both ways: a meeting created, moved or deleted on one side is on the other too.
DoliCalSyncDisabled              = Synchronization is disabled. An administrator can enable it in the setup of DoliCal.
DoliCalSyncNotSecure             = This address is plain http: the password would travel in clear and the iPhone refuses such accounts. Use the https address of your Dolibarr.
DoliCalSyncServer                = Server address
DoliCalSyncPassword              = Your Dolibarr password
DoliCalSyncCalendarUrl           = Direct address of the agenda, if the app asks for it
DoliCalSyncAndroid               = Android (DAVx⁵)
DoliCalSyncAndroid1              = Install the free DAVx⁵ app from the Play Store or F-Droid.
DoliCalSyncAndroid2              = Tap + then "Login with URL and user name".
DoliCalSyncAndroid3              = Paste the server address, your login and your Dolibarr password.
DoliCalSyncAndroid4              = Tick "My Dolibarr agenda": it shows in the calendar of the phone.
DoliCalSyncApple                 = iPhone, iPad and Mac
DoliCalSyncApple1                = Settings › Calendar › Accounts › Add Account › Other.
DoliCalSyncApple2                = Tap "Add CalDAV Account".
DoliCalSyncApple3                = Server: the server address, then your login and your Dolibarr password.
DoliCalSyncApple4                = On a Mac: Calendar › Settings › Accounts › + › Other CalDAV Account, type "Manual".
DoliCalSyncThunderbird           = Thunderbird
DoliCalSyncThunderbird1          = Calendar › New Calendar › On the Network.
DoliCalSyncThunderbird2          = Your Dolibarr login, and the server address as location.
DoliCalSyncThunderbird3          = "Find Calendars", tick your agenda then give your password.
DoliCalSyncWhat                  = What syncs
DoliCalSyncWhat1                 = Your meetings, the ones you organize and the ones you are invited to, with the participants and their answer.
DoliCalSyncWhat2                 = Creating, moving, renaming or deleting a meeting on the phone updates Dolibarr; a repetition created on the phone becomes a series.
DoliCalSyncWhat3                 = Accepting or declining an invitation, and the reminders, both ways. A declined meeting leaves the phone.
DoliCalSyncWhat4                 = The meetings of the last %s days and all the coming ones. Third parties, projects, documents and attachments stay in Dolibarr; the report is copied under the description.
